c Pigeonhole principle: 4 pigeons, 3 holes (UNSAT)
c Variable p_i_j (pigeon i in hole j) = 3*i + j + 1 (1-indexed)
c Pigeons: 0..3, Holes: 0..2
c At-least-one: each pigeon must be in some hole
c At-most-one: no two pigeons in the same hole
p cnf 12 22
c Pigeon 0 must be in some hole
1 2 3 0
c Pigeon 1 must be in some hole
4 5 6 0
c Pigeon 2 must be in some hole
7 8 9 0
c Pigeon 3 must be in some hole
10 11 12 0
c Hole 0: at most one pigeon
-1 -4 0
-1 -7 0
-1 -10 0
-4 -7 0
-4 -10 0
-7 -10 0
